\ cv8-fuse-var.4 - a data word's @ and ! as one operation in code compiled at RUN time (Iteration 687: the gene
\ rtvar; step 3 of results/drafts/search-reopen-plan-677.md - relf's VAR@ and VAR!, its Iteration 260). Loaded
\ after the other fusers of either family (cv8-fuse.4 or cv8t-fuse.4, their -imm, -loopall, -iplus; 689: the two-bit
\ tag too, its codes one byte each - the converter pins vf and vs), before cv8t-empty.4 and cv8t-jit.4, and only for
\ designs with the gene: its code costs image bytes, and only the designs that choose it pay them.
\
\ A call to a data word - its code DOVAR: a VARIABLE, a CREATE - followed straight by @ or ! becomes vf or vs and the
\ slot of its parameter field, the operations the converter lays for the kernel's own variables (spec var): one
\ dispatch for three (the call, DOVAR, the @ or !). The call is laid as before and remembered - VAR-AT where it began,
\ VAR-PFA its parameter field - and LAST-OP is left at VAR-MARK, an address no other rule matches (it is no byte
\ before HERE), so a branch target, which clears LAST-OP, and any operation compiled after the call, which moves it,
\ stop the fusion: nothing is fused across a label (relf's rule). A slot out of the design's reach (23 bits, or 16
\ without VARSLOT) leaves the call. In relf a VAR@ averages 3.2 bytes, about a call and @: dispatches, not bytes.
\
\ VAR-OPS: this design's vf and vs, @ and !, VARSLOT (1: a slot of 2 or 3 big-endian bytes; 0: 2 little-endian),
\ SCALE - written by the converter (tools/layout.py), zeros where the design has no vf (the fusion off). Every
\ COMPILE, not fused goes to the COMPILE,8 before this one (the translator keeps a later X8's call to an earlier X8
\ of its own name).

CREATE VAR-OPS ( --- c-addr )   0 C, 0 C, 0 C, 0 C, 0 C, 0 C, 0 C, 0 C,
ALIGN
VARIABLE VAR-AT ( --- a-addr )     \ where the last call to a data word began
VARIABLE VAR-PFA ( --- a-addr )    \ its parameter field
VARIABLE VAR-MARK ( --- a-addr )   \ LAST-OP's value while that call is the last thing laid

: SLOT-OF ( a-addr --- u -1 | 0 )
\ a's slot - its offset from the image, scaled - if the design's slot operand reaches it.
  START @ - DUP 0< IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  VAR-OPS 5 + C@ ?DUP IF  2DUP 1 SWAP LSHIFT 1- AND IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN  RSHIFT  THEN
  DUP VAR-OPS 4 + C@ IF 8388608 ELSE 65536 THEN < IF -1 EXIT THEN DROP 0 ;

: SLOT, ( u --- )
\ tools/sod16.py's emit_slot.
  VAR-OPS 4 + C@ 0= IF DUP 255 AND C, 8 RSHIFT 255 AND C, EXIT THEN
  DUP 32768 < IF DUP 8 RSHIFT C, 255 AND C, EXIT THEN
  DUP 16 RSHIFT 128 OR C, DUP 8 RSHIFT 255 AND C, 255 AND C, ;

: VAR-FUSE ( xt --- xt 0 | -1 )
\ xt, a primitive, is @ or ! straight after a call to a data word: vf or vs and the slot in the call's place.
  LAST-OP @ VAR-MARK = 0= IF 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP C@ VAR-OPS 2 + C@ = IF VAR-OPS C@ ELSE
    DUP C@ VAR-OPS 3 + C@ = IF VAR-OPS 1+ C@ ELSE 0 EXIT THEN THEN
  VAR-PFA @ SLOT-OF 0= IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  ROT DROP  VAR-AT @ HERE - ALLOT  SWAP OP, SLOT,  0 LAST-OP ! -1 ;

: COMPILE,8 ( xt --- )
\ The COMPILE,8 before this one, with a data word's @ and ! fused, and a call to a data word remembered.
  VAR-OPS C@ 0= IF COMPILE,8 EXIT THEN
  DUP PRIMITIVE? IF VAR-FUSE IF EXIT THEN COMPILE,8 EXIT THEN
  DUP C@ DOVAR-OP = IF
    HERE SWAP DUP >BODY VAR-PFA ! COMPILE,8 VAR-AT ! VAR-MARK LAST-OP ! EXIT
  THEN COMPILE,8 ;
